msgid "(more than one answer can be true)"
msgstr "(aktar minn tweġiba waħda tista’ tkun vera)"

msgid "Ridiculise one's interlocutor in order to have him concede he is wrong."
msgstr "Tirrabja lill-interlokutur tiegħek sabiex iġġiegħlu jammetti li huwa żbaljat."

msgid "No. Socratic irony is not a matter of psychology, it concerns argumentation."
msgstr "Le. L-ironija Sokratika mhix kwistjoni ta’ psikoloġija, iżda tikkonċerna l-argumentazzjoni."

msgid "Admit one's own errors to invite one's interlocutor to do the same."
msgstr "Ammetti l-iżbalji tiegħek stess biex tistieden lill-interlokutur tiegħek jagħmel l-istess."

msgid "No. Socratic irony is not a seduction strategy or a method based on the example."
msgstr "Le. L-ironija Sokratika mhix strateġija ta’ seduzzjoni jew metodu bbażat fuq l-eżempju."

msgid "Compell one's interlocutor, by a series of questions and sub-questions, to admit he doesn't know what he claims to know."
msgstr "Iġġiegħel lill-interlokutur tiegħek, permezz ta’ serje ta’ mistoqsijiet u sottomistoqsijiet, jammetti li ma jafx dak li jiddikjara li jaf."

msgid "Indeed. Socratic irony is an interrogative method. The Greek \"eirotao\" means \"ask questions\""
msgstr "Tabilħaqq. L-ironija Sokratika hija metodu interrogattiv. Il-kelma Griega \"eirotao\" tfisser \"saqsi mistoqsijiet\""

msgid "Use the Principle of Non Contradiction to force one's interlocutor into a dead end."
msgstr "Uża l-Princìpju tan-Non-Kontradizzjoni biex iġġiegħel lill-interlokutur tiegħek f’rotta magħluqa."

msgid "This answer is not false. It is true that the revelation of the interlocutor's ignorance means showing the contradictory conclusions where lead his premisses."
msgstr "Din it-tweġiba mhix falza. Huwa veru li r-rivelazzjoni tal-injoranza tal-interlokutur tfisser li turi l-konklużjonijiet kontradittorji li wasslu għalihom il-premessi tiegħu."

