msgid "Split users' upload directory"
msgstr "Aqsam id-direttorju tal-uploads tal-utenti"

msgid "On high-load portals, where a lot of users are registered and send their pictures, the upload directory (main/upload/users/) might contain too many files for the filesystem to handle (it has been reported with more than 36000 files on a Debian server). Changing this option will enable a one-level splitting of the directories in the upload directory. 9 directories will be used in the base directory and all subsequent users' directories will be stored into one of these 9 directories. The change of this option will not affect the directories structure on disk, but will affect the behaviour of the Chamilo code, so if you change this option, you have to create the new directories and move the existing directories by yourself on te server. Be aware that when creating and moving those directories, you will have to move the directories of users 1 to 9 into subdirectories of the same name. If you are not sure about this option, it is best not to activate it."
msgstr "Fuq portali b'tagħbija għolja, fejn ħafna utenti huma reġistrati u jibagħtu r-ritratti tagħhom, id-direttorju tal-uploads (main/upload/users/) jista' jkun fih wisq fajls għas-sistema tal-fajls biex timmaniġġjah (ġie rrappurtat b'aktar minn 36000 fajl fuq server Debian). Il-bidla ta' din l-għażla se tippermetti qsim ta' livell wieħed tad-direttorji fid-direttorju tal-uploads. 9 direttorji se jintużaw fid-direttorju bażi u d-direttorji kollha sussegwenti tal-utenti se jinħażnu f'wieħed minn dawn id-9 direttorji. Il-bidla ta' din l-għażla ma taffettwax l-istruttura tad-direttorji fuq id-diska, iżda taffettwa l-imġiba tal-kodiċi ta' Chamilo, għalhekk jekk tibdel din l-għażla, trid toħloq id-direttorji ġodda u tmexxi d-direttorji eżistenti int stess fuq is-server. Kun konxju li meta toħloq u tmexxi dawk id-direttorji, trid tmexxi d-direttorji tal-utenti 1 sa 9 f'sottodirettorji bl-istess isem. Jekk m'intix ċert dwar din l-għażla, aħjar ma tattivahiex."

