msgid "Survey Help"
msgstr "Għajnuna għas-Sondaġġ"

msgid "<p>Getting proper feedback on your courses is extremely important. You will find the dedicated Survey tool invaluable for getting effective feedback from users. </p> <p><b>Creating a new survey</b></p> <p> Click on the link 'Create a new survey' and fill in the fields 'Survey code' and 'Survey title'. With the help of the calendar, you can control the duration of your survey. There's no need to keep it open for a whole year; allow access for a few days at the end of the course program. Filling in the text fields 'Survey introduction' and 'Survey thanks' is also good practice; this will add clarity and a certain friendliness to your survey.</p> <p><b>Adding questions to the survey</b></p> <p>Once the survey outline is created, it is up to you to create the questions. The 'Survey' tool has many question types: open/closed questions, percentage, QCM, multiple responses... You should certainly find everything you need for your (ever increasing) feedback requirements.</p>  <p><b>Previewing the survey</b></p><p>Once you have created questions, you may want to check what the survey will look like to learners. Click on the 'Preview' icon and the preview screen will show you exactly this.</p> <p><b>Publishing the survey</b></p> <p>Happy with the preview? Any modifications to be made? No? Then click on the icon 'Publish survey' to send the survey to the selected list of recipients. As with creating groups, use the list 'Users of this course' on the left and the one for 'receivers' on its right to arrange this. Next, fill in the e-mail subject 'Title of the e-mail' and the content, 'Text of the e-mail'. Potential surveyees will be alerted by e-mail of the availability of a survey. Think carefully about  the wording of the e-mail  because it will play a big part in motivating users to take the survey.</p>  <p><b>Survey reports</b></p> Analysing surveys is a tedious task. The survey Reporting tool will help with analysis as it sorts reports according to question, user, comparisons etc...  <p><b>Managing surveys</b></p> When managing surveys you will see some new icons, apart from the usual 'Edit' and 'Delete' options. You can preview, publish and keep track of your surveys and responses using these.</p>"
msgstr "<p>Li tikseb feedback xieraq fuq il-korsijiet tiegħek huwa estremament importanti. Se ssib l-għodda ddedikata tas-Sondaġġi ta' valur kbir biex tikseb feedback effettiv mill-utenti. </p> <p><b>Ħolqien ta' sondaġġ ġdid</b></p> <p> Ikklikkja fuq il-link 'Oħloq sondaġġ ġdid' u imla l-oqsma 'Kodiċi tas-sondaġġ' u 'Titlu tas-sondaġġ'. Bl-għajnuna tal-kalendarju, tista' tikkontrolla t-tul tas-sondaġġ tiegħek. M'hemmx bżonn li tżommu miftuħ għal sena sħiħa; ħalli aċċess għal ftit jiem fl-aħħar tal-programm tal-kors. Li timla l-oqsma tat-test 'Introduzzjoni tas-sondaġġ' u 'Grazzi tas-sondaġġ' hija wkoll prattika tajba; dan iżid ċarezza u ċerta ħbiberija mas-sondaġġ tiegħek.</p> <p><b>Żieda ta' mistoqsijiet mas-sondaġġ</b></p> <p>Ladarba l-kontorn tas-sondaġġ ikun ġie maħluq, huwa f'idejk li toħloq il-mistoqsijiet. L-għodda 'Sondaġġ' għandha ħafna tipi ta' mistoqsijiet: mistoqsijiet miftuħa/magħluqa, perċentwali, QCM, risposti multipli... Żgur li ssib dak kollu li għandek bżonn għar-rekwiżiti tal-feedback tiegħek (li dejjem qed jiżdiedu).</p>  <p><b>Previżjoni tas-sondaġġ</b></p><p>Ladarba tkun ħloqt mistoqsijiet, jista' jkun li trid tiċċekkja kif se jidher is-sondaġġ għall-istudenti. Ikklikkja fuq l-ikona 'Previżjoni' u l-iskrin tal-previżjoni juri eżattament dan.</p> <p><b>Pubblikazzjoni tas-sondaġġ</b></p> <p>Kuntent bil-previżjoni? Xi modifiki x'tagħmel? Le? Imbagħad ikklikkja fuq l-ikona 'Ippubblika s-sondaġġ' biex tibgħat is-sondaġġ lil-lista magħżula ta' riċevituri. Bħal meta toħloq gruppi, uża l-lista 'Utenti ta' dan il-kors' fuq ix-xellug u dik għar-'riċevituri' fuq il-lemin biex tirranġa dan. Imbagħad, imla s-suġġett tal-email 'Titlu tal-email' u l-kontenut, 'Test tal-email'. Dawk li jistgħu jkunu mistqarrin jiġu allertati bl-email dwar id-disponibbiltà ta' sondaġġ. Aħseb bir-reqqa dwar il-kliem tal-email għax dan ikollu sehem kbir fil-motivazzjoni tal-utenti biex jieħdu s-sondaġġ.</p>  <p><b>Rapporti tas-sondaġġ</b></p> L-analiżi tas-sondaġġi hija kompitu tedjuz. L-għodda tar-Rappurtar tas-sondaġġi tgħin bl-analiżi billi tissortja r-rapporti skont il-mistoqsija, l-utent, il-komparazzjonijiet eċċ...  <p><b>Ġestjoni tas-sondaġġi</b></p> Meta tmexxi s-sondaġġi tara xi ikoni ġodda, apparti mill-għażliet tas-soltu 'Editja' u 'Ħassar'. Tista' tara l-previżjoni, tippubblika u ssegwi s-sondaġġi u r-risposti tiegħek billi tuża dawn.</p>"

msgid "Project help"
msgstr "Għajnuna għall-Proġett"

msgid "<p> The Project tool facilitates collaborative project work. </p> One way to use the tool is to use it to assign authors charged with keeping written reports on activities throughout the day/week. </p> Coupled with this is a task management tool through which you can assign a relevant task  to any of the designated authors (eg to report on the evolution of safety standards in the business). </p> An item representing new content is called an <i> article </i>. To create a new article, just follow the link in the menu prompting you to do. To edit (if you are the author of the article) or add a comment to an article, just click on the title of this article. </p>"
msgstr "<p> L-għodda tal-Proġett tiffaċilita x-xogħol kollaborattiv fuq proġetti. </p> Mod wieħed kif tuża l-għodda huwa li tużaha biex tassenja awturi inkarigati li jżommu rapporti bil-miktub dwar l-attivitajiet matul il-ġurnata/ġimgħa. </p> Marbut ma' dan hemm għodda ta' ġestjoni tal-kompiti li permezz tagħha tista' tassenja kompitu rilevanti lil kwalunkwe wieħed mill-awturi ddeżinjati (eż. biex tirrapporta dwar l-evoluzzjoni tal-istandards tas-sigurtà fin-negozju). </p> Oġġett li jirrappreżenta kontenut ġdid jissejjaħ <i> artiklu </i>. Biex toħloq artiklu ġdid, segwi biss il-link fil-menu li jistednek tagħmel dan. Biex teditja (jekk int l-awtur tal-artiklu) jew iżżid kumment ma' artiklu, ikklikkja biss fuq it-titlu ta' dan l-artiklu. </p>"

